  "description": "The main window's screens: they may call the app's own commands (window size by name, tray labels, pairing, the move, a help code, picking up after a restart, Quick Send, whether an update is out and installing it, this laptop's name, the Phase 2 screens' view and their checked intents, and the 2.9 deliverables: work checks, repairing what failed, changes after approval, the safe stopping point and the recovery kit), each granted by name and taking typed arguments only; listen to the app's own events (pairing and move updates); and open our own site in the browser. Nothing else.",
